{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_10_agent_handoff_invariant_18", "label": "Invariant 18 \u2014 Galedra runs no model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "label": "Stage 31 \u2014 The rules on the wire, not in the skill (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Owner request: reinstalling a connector after every rule change is unrealistic in production. MCP has no \"fetch the rules from a URL\" mechanism because the server is already that URL, so the answer is one source served over the two live channels \u2014 every tool result, and GET /api/v1/guidance \u2014 with the skill carrying none of it."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_size_rule_or_bug", "label": "The size rule's `or` limb \u2014 a rule that could not fire", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\"Under 3,000 words of input, OR under about 25 claims\" joined two limbs by `or`, and the second limb is the assistant's own output: deciding to record thirteen claims was what made recording thirteen claims permitted. A two-hour, fourteen-chapter transcript went through record_investigation as thirteen claims. The rule is now stated on the input alone."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_results_channel", "label": "Tool results are the only channel with no staleness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The skill is never re-read until a user reinstalls; initialize instructions are reportedly discarded by claude.ai; tool descriptions are cached from the last connection and reportedly truncated near 500 characters. Results are never cached, so every operational rule rides on them, each naming its topic and version; descriptions repeat only what survives truncation and are not what the code relies on."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_thin_skill", "label": "The thin skill points rather than repeats", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cut from ~12 KB to 3.2 KB, keeping only what cannot arrive in a result \u2014 what Galedra is, the galedra: trigger, search first \u2014 and saying that where the skill and the live guidance differ, the guidance wins. Two rules are repeated anyway (your own reasoning is never evidence; never record claims about identifiable private individuals) because an assistant can break both before its first tool call and both damage the record rather than merely producing a worse answer. A spec fails if an operational rule migrates back."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_version_advisory", "label": "Guidance::VERSION is advisory, never enforced", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It tells a host showing guidance to a person whether their copy is current. No tool refuses a call because an assistant last read an older version; that would punish the assistant for the host's caching."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_size_rule_or_bug", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_results_channel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_thin_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_version_advisory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_stage", "target": "app_services_guidance_guidance", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-31-guidance-on-the-wire.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_31_guidance_on_the_wire_results_channel", "target": "app_services_mcp_server_server", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRA